- `perMessageDeflate: false` unless you have measured the need: compression costs CPU per message on the hot path and introduces the permessage-deflate CRIME-style attack surface with secrets in messages. Turn it on for text-heavy, large frames only.
- `maxPayload` is a hard DoS control. A frame larger than it is closed with code `1009`.

**Frame anatomy** (what a WebSocket library is doing for you)
```
byte 0:  FIN(1) RSV1-3(3)  opcode(4)
byte 1:  MASK(1)  payload-len(7)   [126 â†’ next 2 bytes = length; 127 â†’ next 8 bytes = length]
[4 bytes masking key, clientâ†’server frames only]
payload
```
| Opcode | Meaning | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| `0x0` continuation | rest of a fragmented message | reassemble before dispatch |
| `0x1` text | UTF-8 text | serverâ†’client frames are NOT masked |
| `0x2` binary | bytes | decide the app framing yourself |
| `0x8` close | close handshake, carries a 2-byte code + reason | the polite way to end |
| `0x9` ping | liveness probe | serverâ†’client only |
| `0xA` pong | reply to ping | may also come unsolicited |

- **Masking** is mandatory clientâ†’server (proxies must not see your payloads) and forbidden serverâ†’client. A correct server must reject unmasked client frames (`1002` protocol error).
- **Control frames** must be â‰¤125 bytes, cannot be fragmented, and may be interleaved between fragments of a data message.
- **Fragmentation:** large messages arrive as `opcode 0x1, FIN=0`, then `0x0, FIN=0`, ... then `0x0, FIN=1`. A buggy or malicious peer can hold an incomplete message forever â†’ cap the reassembly buffer (this is why `maxPayload` matters).

**Close codes you must handle**
| Code | Name | Meaning to you |
|---|---|---|
| 1000 | normal | clean |
| 1001 | going away | server restart/deploy â†’ client should reconnect; make this deliberate |
| 1002 | protocol error | your client sent an invalid frame |
| 1008 | policy violation | auth failure or message too big |
| 1009 | message too big | `maxPayload` exceeded |
| 1011 | internal error | unexpected server failure |
| 1013 | try again later | server overloaded â€” use this instead of accepting then failing |
| 1015 | TLS handshake | reserved, must not be sent |
| 4000â€“4999 | application | private range: `4001 unauthorized`, `4003 rate-limited`, `4008 session-expired` |

**Connection state machine**
```
